    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just hard to see the \"freedom\" in it when everyone else is so terrified of it. people act like choosing to leave is some ultimate failure or a loss of control, but it actually feels like the only way to actually have control over anything. if I'm just a passenger in this life, isn't the only real way to exert my will to just... pull the plug? it seems so much more logical than just continuing to suffer through a cycle that doesn't end.",
